WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.375
- Yo. are you up?
- Yeah.

3
00:01:28.732 --> 00:01:30.437
Jax has got the jump on you tomorrow.

4
00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:32.728
Two bell.

5
00:01:35.702 --> 00:01:36.776
I figure I owe you.

6
00:01:40.281 --> 00:01:42.449
Yo. Did you hear what I said?

7
00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:45.327
I heard.

8
00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:51.649
Thanks.

9
00:02:12.271 --> 00:02:15.732
Everybody down now! On the ground!

10
00:02:16.651 --> 00:02:18.735
You! Inmate! On the ground!

11
00:02:20.112 --> 00:02:21.112
Down!

12
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.691
- Get down!
- You heard him!

13
00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:26.910
On the fucking ground!

14
00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:53.228
You're up.

15
00:02:55.815 --> 00:02:57.232
To your left.

16
00:03:00.194 --> 00:03:01.695
On the line.

17
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.704
All right...

18
00:03:11.038 --> 00:03:12.872
Step to the right.

19
00:03:24.885 --> 00:03:26.553
Let's go.

20
00:03:34.395 --> 00:03:35.595
Hands.

21
00:03:40.985 --> 00:03:42.152
Enjoy.

22
00:04:49.136 --> 00:04:50.553
Against the wall.

23
00:04:54.308 --> 00:04:55.475
Let's go.

24
00:05:31.679 --> 00:05:34.305
Lunchtime. inmate. Eat your veggies.

25
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.482
There you go.

26
00:05:46.527 --> 00:05:47.902
Hey. Roag!

27
00:05:48.696 --> 00:05:49.696
Yeah?

28
00:05:50.114 --> 00:05:51.110
Got the time?

29
00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.275
Fuck you care? You got a date?

30
00:05:53.375 --> 00:05:54.375
No.

31
00:05:54.785 --> 00:05:57.412
Maybe you got a sister or a cousin?

32
00:05:58.539 --> 00:06:00.782
Wanna get your head smashed?

33
00:06:00.882 --> 00:06:02.208
No. not really.

34
00:06:04.378 --> 00:06:05.461
It's five to 4:00.

35
00:06:07.464 --> 00:06:08.882
Wise ass.

36
00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:16.598
Hey. Fruitcake! Let's go.

37
00:06:19.018 --> 00:06:22.979
Two... Three... Four...

38
00:06:24.398 --> 00:06:27.525
Five... Six... Seven...

39
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.402
Eight...

40
00:06:30.738 --> 00:06:31.738
Nine...

41
00:06:32.323 --> 00:06:33.523
Ten...

42
00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.430
290... 291...

43
00:06:43.542 --> 00:06:46.142
292... 293...

44
00:06:47.671 --> 00:06:48.871
294...

45
00:06:49.673 --> 00:06:52.273
295... 296...

46
00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.860
297... 298...

47
00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.630
299... 300.

48
00:07:02.019 --> 00:07:03.645
What the fuck...

49
00:07:06.106 --> 00:07:07.106
Come on!

50
00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:20.036
- You okay?
- I got everybody. I got everybody.

51
00:07:23.999 --> 00:07:25.450
What the fuck's going on?

52
00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.328
We've got a fire. gate two.
All prisoners back to their cells.

53
00:07:28.428 --> 00:07:29.796
Copy that.

54
00:07:34.134 --> 00:07:35.718
What the fuck...

55
00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:39.347
We got a runner!
Repeat. prisoner is running!

56
00:07:43.727 --> 00:07:44.978
Let's go. let's go!

57
00:08:03.664 --> 00:08:04.998
Nice look.

58
00:08:05.165 --> 00:08:06.249
Hush's idea.

59
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.167
Nice. right?

60
00:08:08.335 --> 00:08:09.577
How was inside. boss man?

61
00:08:09.677 --> 00:08:12.255
Inside's great. Everyone's asking about you.

62
00:08:13.465 --> 00:08:16.843
If you weren't out soon. I'd be breaking into
that motherfucker and pulling your ass out.

63
00:08:17.094 --> 00:08:20.046
Only ex-con I know gets out.
wants to go back in.

64
00:08:20.146 --> 00:08:22.924
I didn't say "wants." I said I would.

65
00:08:23.024 --> 00:08:25.143
There is a difference.

66
00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:49.167
Don't spend it all in one place.

67
00:09:01.138 --> 00:09:03.890
We have an escape
from Bendwater Penitentiary.

68
00:09:20.074 --> 00:09:21.900
Step out of the booth
with your hands in the air!

69
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.534
Showtime.

70
00:09:26.246 --> 00:09:28.406
Put your hands in the air! Now!

71
00:09:28.506 --> 00:09:30.992
- Get them up. now!
- Hands in the air!

72
00:09:31.092 --> 00:09:35.671
Put your hands on your head!
Interlock your fingers! Do not move!

73
00:09:36.924 --> 00:09:38.716
Beautiful day.

74
00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.319
What the hell is going on here?

75
00:10:06.419 --> 00:10:09.247
Calm down. Warden. I'm Lester Clark.

76
00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.251
I'm the CEO of B&C Security.

77
00:10:13.794 --> 00:10:16.254
You might have heard of us. No?

78
00:10:17.965 --> 00:10:21.209
All right. well...
We're an independent security company

79
00:10:21.309 --> 00:10:24.887
hired by the Federal Bureau of Prisons

80
00:10:25.764 --> 00:10:31.310
to test the integrity of their
maximum security facilities nationwide.

81
00:10:33.397 --> 00:10:38.401
This is Ray Breslin.
He's my partner and resident Houdini.

82
00:10:39.069 --> 00:10:40.069
Warden.

83
00:10:41.238 --> 00:10:44.274
For the last seven years.
Ray has been inserted into

84
00:10:44.374 --> 00:10:48.953
every maximum incarceration facility
in the system.

85
00:10:49.413 --> 00:10:52.198
He is there to ensure
that each and every one of them

86
00:10:52.298 --> 00:10:54.834
is 100% escape-proof.

87
00:10:55.502 --> 00:11:00.089
And apparently yours wasn't.
and he got out.

88
00:11:02.718 --> 00:11:04.135
Okay. fine.

89
00:11:08.515 --> 00:11:10.308
I suppose you're gonna tell me
how you did it?

90
00:11:11.143 --> 00:11:13.352
Think he wants to know?
Doesn't seem like it.

91
00:11:16.607 --> 00:11:18.933
Ray. you're on.

92
00:11:19.033 --> 00:11:20.818
Warden. let's start from the top.

93
00:11:20.944 --> 00:11:23.938
Any break requires three things.
knowing the layout.

94
00:11:24.038 --> 00:11:27.325
understanding the routine.
and help from outside or in.

95
00:11:28.327 --> 00:11:30.445
If you know the layout.
the weak side is obvious.

96
00:11:30.545 --> 00:11:33.781
In Bendwater's case.
it's the Secure Housing Unit.

97
00:11:33.881 --> 00:11:37.952
The government expenditure
was 17 million dollars building that facility.

98
00:11:38.052 --> 00:11:40.046
It's state-of-the-art.

99
00:11:40.839 --> 00:11:45.551
The only problem is.
it's located next to an unsecured fire garage.

100
00:11:48.972 --> 00:11:52.266
First I needed to get inside.
so I made some enemies.

101
00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.223
Once inside.
it was obvious you were short-staffed.

102
00:11:58.323 --> 00:12:00.725
Federal guidelines recommend
two guards are present

103
00:12:00.825 --> 00:12:04.395
when transferring high risk inmates.
You only use one.

104
00:12:04.495 --> 00:12:06.656
Knowing the guards' routine
was the next step.

105
00:12:07.366 --> 00:12:11.244
Thirty seconds into my rec time.
my CO took a smoke break.

106
00:12:11.578 --> 00:12:14.914
For seven minutes every day.
there were no eyes on me.

107
00:12:15.249 --> 00:12:16.415
Two...

108
00:12:17.751 --> 00:12:18.747
Three...

109
00:12:18.847 --> 00:12:21.921
After I knew the routine.
all I had to do was pick the day

110
00:12:22.839 --> 00:12:26.292
and arrange for a distraction
at the front gate for exactly 4:00 p.m.

111
00:12:26.392 --> 00:12:29.337
But at this point.
you were still locked inside a steel box.

112
00:12:29.437 --> 00:12:32.098
To get out. you had to have a key code.

113
00:12:32.599 --> 00:12:34.600
You have very good chocolate milk.

114
00:12:37.604 --> 00:12:40.773
See. the cartons
contain a thin layer of wax laminate.

115
00:12:46.571 --> 00:12:47.772
Lay it over the keypad.

116
00:12:47.872 --> 00:12:50.783
the impression will indicate
which four keys were pressed.

117
00:13:03.588 --> 00:13:07.709
With the four keys. it's just a numbers game
to identify the correct sequence.

118
00:13:07.809 --> 00:13:09.802
I just needed to get to the keypad.

119
00:13:30.991 --> 00:13:33.443
After I covered my tracks.
I had one minute to make it

120
00:13:33.543 --> 00:13:36.746
to the fire response
shed before the team did.

121
00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:51.669
I knew the guards were still on the roof
doing what they do. which is wasting time.

122
00:13:51.769 --> 00:13:52.970
What the fuck are you saying?

123
00:13:55.849 --> 00:13:58.017
And before you know it.
I'm right where I want to be.

124
00:14:08.487 --> 00:14:10.613
Just in time to catch my ride.

125
00:14:20.332 --> 00:14:22.950
Then your men
drove me right off the grounds.

126
00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.919
You have any questions?

127
00:14:25.545 --> 00:14:27.545
Yeah. One.

128
00:14:31.218 --> 00:14:35.296
What kind of man would choose to spend
most of his life in prison?

129
00:14:35.396 --> 00:14:38.015
Don't take it personally. Warden.

130
00:14:39.309 --> 00:14:42.804
Over the years. Ray has broken out of
14 of these institutions.

131
00:14:42.904 --> 00:14:46.724
Some people have a talent to paint.
some to sing.

132
00:14:46.824 --> 00:14:48.067
Me. I sing.

133
00:14:48.735 --> 00:14:51.938
Ray Breslin. he possesses
a unique set of skills.

134
00:14:52.038 --> 00:14:55.574
He is able to break out of
any prison designed by man.

135
00:14:57.577 --> 00:14:58.986
So have you been good?

136
00:14:59.086 --> 00:15:01.447
Yeah. You? You a good boy inside?

137
00:15:01.547 --> 00:15:02.957
Of course.

138
00:15:03.542 --> 00:15:06.994
Okay... How did that thing with that guy go?

139
00:15:07.094 --> 00:15:08.671
- What guy?
- What guy?

140
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:12.083
When I was going in. you were about to
have dinner with some guy. some bozo.

141
00:15:12.183 --> 00:15:15.094
Oh. yeah. That bozo ended before dessert.

142
00:15:16.513 --> 00:15:17.672
Well. that's his loss.

143
00:15:17.772 --> 00:15:19.849
Yeah. They're all losers.

144
00:15:20.517 --> 00:15:22.184
How many times have I told you that?

145
00:15:23.103 --> 00:15:25.187
You want to get something to eat
when we get back?

146
00:15:27.441 --> 00:15:28.816
Is there a problem?

147
00:15:32.279 --> 00:15:34.321
You're a horrible cook.

148
00:15:34.865 --> 00:15:38.284
That's nice.
Well. you can complain in the morning.

149
00:15:39.619 --> 00:15:40.619
Ouch.

150
00:15:48.962 --> 00:15:50.796
Morning. sir. How can I help you?

151
00:15:54.468 --> 00:15:56.711
Mr. Breslin. I'm so sorry. I'm Jules.

152
00:15:56.811 --> 00:15:59.305
That's okay. You're new here?

153
00:15:59.806 --> 00:16:01.674
No. sir. I've been here five months.

154
00:16:01.774 --> 00:16:03.642
- Five months?
- Yes. sir.

155
00:16:06.897 --> 00:16:08.814
What do you got for me?

156
00:16:09.274 --> 00:16:10.733
Check it out.

157
00:16:13.153 --> 00:16:15.321
That's good. Very smart.

158
00:16:15.989 --> 00:16:20.159
Did you do this all by yourself?
I'm impressed. Genius.

159
00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.161
You're smart. but...

160
00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.332
Sorry. not smart enough.

161
00:16:28.293 --> 00:16:29.668
Don't be bitter.

162
00:16:48.855 --> 00:16:51.857
Mr. Breslin. they're ready for you
in the conference room.

163
00:16:55.528 --> 00:16:57.279
Morning. Les. Abby.

164
00:16:58.281 --> 00:17:02.826
Jessica Mayer. It's an honor to meet you.
Your work is the gold standard in the field.

165
00:17:03.328 --> 00:17:05.037
What you've accomplished is remarkable.

166
00:17:08.917 --> 00:17:11.535
Thank you. And you're here because...

167
00:17:11.635 --> 00:17:13.371
She's Agency. Ray. As in...

168
00:17:13.471 --> 00:17:15.047
Central Intelligence Agency.

169
00:17:15.215 --> 00:17:16.249
You a spy?

170
00:17:16.349 --> 00:17:18.300
Worse. I'm a lawyer.

171
00:17:19.552 --> 00:17:24.223
Ray. hear her out. She's legit.
I called Langley myself.

172
00:17:25.392 --> 00:17:28.143
Fine. I'll just listen. Go ahead.

173
00:17:29.479 --> 00:17:33.474
Mr. Breslin. after ending "extraordinary
rendition." the Agency is looking for

174
00:17:33.574 --> 00:17:36.477
alternate situations for
incarcerating the sort of people

175
00:17:36.577 --> 00:17:40.072
who commit acts so despicable
they're best... Well. how can I put it?

176
00:17:40.532 --> 00:17:41.657
Eliminated?

177
00:17:42.575 --> 00:17:45.611
Disappeared.
And we're currently testing a prototype

178
00:17:45.711 --> 00:17:48.406
to deal with people
no government wants on their books.

179
00:17:48.506 --> 00:17:51.659
But first and foremost.
the people financing this need to know

180
00:17:51.759 --> 00:17:53.619
these facilities are escape-proof

181
00:17:53.719 --> 00:17:55.997
before the whole system
goes online globally.

182
00:17:56.097 --> 00:17:59.800
What she's really saying is that none of this
is officially sanctioned by anyone.

183
00:18:00.218 --> 00:18:01.294
Close.

184
00:18:01.394 --> 00:18:02.503
What I'm saying. Miss Ross.

185
00:18:02.603 --> 00:18:06.340
is that these facilities
are privately funded and administered.

186
00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.634
So the word "official" does not really apply.

187
00:18:08.734 --> 00:18:09.726
So if anything goes wrong.

188
00:18:09.826 --> 00:18:11.804
nothing comes back to
bite you people in the ass.

189
00:18:11.904 --> 00:18:14.140
This is not your concern.

190
00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.442
Hey! I owe him. I don't owe you.

191
00:18:17.569 --> 00:18:21.238
My job is to make sure
the United States is safe and clean.

192
00:18:21.448 --> 00:18:23.699
All right. can we just cut the crap
and call it like it is?

193
00:18:24.034 --> 00:18:27.194
These institutions are off the grid.
There are no trials. there's no convictions.

194
00:18:27.294 --> 00:18:29.363
These people are just disappeared.

195
00:18:29.463 --> 00:18:31.498
And you want him to go in and test it?

196
00:18:32.625 --> 00:18:36.203
Maybe it's time for me to interject into
the conversation that they have offered

197
00:18:36.303 --> 00:18:39.882
double your standard fee.
that's five mil. right? In advance.

198
00:18:40.216 --> 00:18:41.667
So you like this?

199
00:18:41.767 --> 00:18:44.628
Look. I'm a numbers guy.
You're the artist. Ray.

200
00:18:44.728 --> 00:18:47.973
From a financial standpoint. I like it.
Yes. I like it very much.

201
00:18:49.601 --> 00:18:51.477
Beyond the money. Mr. Breslin.

202
00:18:51.936 --> 00:18:53.387
the people that are sent to this place

203
00:18:53.487 --> 00:18:55.890
should not be allowed out
into the real world.

204
00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:59.651
Every one of them
is a potential game changer. For the worse.

205
00:18:59.944 --> 00:19:00.986
All right.

206
00:19:05.533 --> 00:19:06.567
Guidelines?

207
00:19:06.667 --> 00:19:10.829
The usual. Full work. Alias. Cover story.
Contact. Evac number. Right?

208
00:19:10.997 --> 00:19:14.742
Well. the only difference is
to fully test the security of the system

209
00:19:14.842 --> 00:19:17.753
it's essential that none of you
know the location of the incarceration.

210
00:19:19.172 --> 00:19:20.623
Will that present a problem?

211
00:19:20.723 --> 00:19:22.007
Yes. Yes. it would.

212
00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.268
When do we start?

213
00:19:33.686 --> 00:19:34.853
We just did.

214
00:19:37.857 --> 00:19:41.352
You and your new identity
will be picked up from this location

215
00:19:41.452 --> 00:19:44.279
by private contractors 24 hours from now.

216
00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.126
I don't like this.

217
00:20:05.226 --> 00:20:06.226
And you don't like her.

218
00:20:06.344 --> 00:20:07.970
Don't flatter yourself.

219
00:20:09.097 --> 00:20:11.590
We're going against
every protocol and guideline

220
00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.428
that you yourself have insisted on
every single time that you've gone in.

221
00:20:15.528 --> 00:20:16.637
And I don't like her.

222
00:20:16.737 --> 00:20:18.556
You're right.
There's nothing to like about any of it.

223
00:20:18.656 --> 00:20:21.559
- Then why do it?
- Because he's ambitious and greedy.

224
00:20:21.659 --> 00:20:24.236
You say that like it's a bad thing.

225
00:20:25.405 --> 00:20:26.864
Profile.

226
00:20:28.116 --> 00:20:32.578
Name. Anthony Portos. Born Madrid.
Mother died when you were 13.

227
00:20:33.872 --> 00:20:35.739
Raised by your father in the U.S.

228
00:20:35.839 --> 00:20:38.451
You were suspected of
manufacturing bombs that have been used

229
00:20:38.551 --> 00:20:41.620
in a dozen political bombings
across Europe and South America

230
00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.330
for the last 10 years.

231
00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.715
Contact on site?

232
00:20:45.216 --> 00:20:47.251
Warden's name is Roger Marsh.

233
00:20:47.351 --> 00:20:48.343
Evacuation code?

234
00:20:48.443 --> 00:20:50.053
3-1-0-2-7-5.

235
00:20:55.351 --> 00:20:56.427
All right. Let's do it.

236
00:20:56.527 --> 00:20:57.519
Tag him.

237
00:20:57.619 --> 00:20:59.472
No. I don't need this. Really.

238
00:20:59.572 --> 00:21:01.015
Yeah. you do. It's non-negotiable.

239
00:21:01.115 --> 00:21:02.858
You think I'm letting you go in cold?

240
00:21:03.067 --> 00:21:04.234
This gets old.

241
00:21:05.445 --> 00:21:06.528
Man the fuck up.

242
00:21:07.447 --> 00:21:08.522
Try it some time.

243
00:21:08.622 --> 00:21:11.025
Sounds good. boss man.
Any time you want to retire...

244
00:21:11.125 --> 00:21:13.360
I've been takin' notes. I'm ready to step up.

245
00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.121
Where am I gonna find another techno-thug
as gifted as you?

246
00:21:16.247 --> 00:21:17.222
Freak of nature.

247
00:21:17.322 --> 00:21:18.457
Yeah. very rare.

248
00:21:22.545 --> 00:21:25.130
There you are. baby. Transponder's good.

249
00:21:26.299 --> 00:21:28.959
It's like having me right on your shoulder.

250
00:21:29.059 --> 00:21:30.552
Where else?

251
00:21:35.975 --> 00:21:38.810
Hey. don't forget to write us. All right?

252
00:22:46.421 --> 00:22:47.421
Shit!

253
00:23:23.082 --> 00:23:24.333
Hold it!

254
00:23:41.851 --> 00:23:43.602
Put him to sleep.

255
00:26:36.943 --> 00:26:40.529
Prisoner 7458. Anthony Portos.

256
00:26:42.782 --> 00:26:46.409
Welcome to the International
Detainee Unit intake.

257
00:26:47.119 --> 00:26:48.328
I'm Warden Hobbes.

258
00:26:48.746 --> 00:26:51.289
Hobbes. Where's Warden Marsh?

259
00:26:52.041 --> 00:26:54.584
There is no Warden Marsh.

260
00:27:01.092 --> 00:27:02.843
What. am I disoriented? Is that it?

261
00:27:03.845 --> 00:27:05.462
I guess that must be it.

262
00:27:05.562 --> 00:27:08.382
And I didn't see a man
killed on a transport helicopter

263
00:27:08.482 --> 00:27:10.809
and thrown out either. right?

264
00:27:15.773 --> 00:27:18.733
Mr. Portos. your intake is finished.

265
00:27:19.652 --> 00:27:20.652
Wait!

266
00:27:20.987 --> 00:27:23.613
My evacuation code is 3-1-0-2-7-5.

267
00:27:24.991 --> 00:27:26.316
Evacuation code?

268
00:27:26.416 --> 00:27:28.151
Yes. Evacuation code.

269
00:27:28.251 --> 00:27:32.914
Meaning you give me a number
and you walk out of here free as a bird?

270
00:27:34.959 --> 00:27:37.836
No. I don't think so.

271
00:27:40.965 --> 00:27:44.259
You're here now. And you belong to me.

272
00:27:47.513 --> 00:27:49.514
Your intake is finished.

273
00:27:50.057 --> 00:27:52.851
Wait... I have an evacuation code!

274
00:27:53.185 --> 00:27:54.181
Anything?

275
00:27:54.281 --> 00:27:57.055
Getting a ghost bounce. same as yesterday.
I can't find him.

276
00:27:57.155 --> 00:27:59.141
You ran a full diagnostic on the system?

277
00:27:59.241 --> 00:28:00.358
Twice.

278
00:28:00.776 --> 00:28:02.068
Run it again.

279
00:28:05.948 --> 00:28:08.867
All prisoners A-Block proceed to Babylon.

280
00:28:09.869 --> 00:28:13.038
All prisoners A-Block
to proceed to Babylon.

281
00:28:29.889 --> 00:28:31.139
Portos.

282
00:29:13.724 --> 00:29:16.643
Everybody's days are numbered in Babylon!

283
00:29:22.274 --> 00:29:25.110
Babylon. death. death!

284
00:29:42.086 --> 00:29:43.086
Hey!

285
00:29:44.839 --> 00:29:47.173
Go make some friends.
You're gonna need them.

286
00:30:09.488 --> 00:30:10.488
Hey!

287
00:30:44.982 --> 00:30:48.026
Stay down! Stay down!

288
00:31:15.721 --> 00:31:18.098
New fish. We own you!

289
00:31:21.477 --> 00:31:22.727
Back off!

290
00:31:30.194 --> 00:31:31.402
Last time.

291
00:31:33.739 --> 00:31:35.365
Back away.

292
00:31:41.205 --> 00:31:42.205
Portos.

293
00:31:45.042 --> 00:31:47.335
Rottmayer. Emil Rottmayer.

294
00:31:48.671 --> 00:31:51.256
Really not much
in a hand-shaking mood right now.

295
00:31:53.384 --> 00:31:54.384
Okay.

296
00:31:56.011 --> 00:31:57.671
Your name.

297
00:31:57.771 --> 00:32:01.057
The fourth Musketeer. It's a good name.

298
00:32:04.770 --> 00:32:06.521
Why are you in here?

299
00:32:08.357 --> 00:32:09.524
Why do you care?

300
00:32:09.775 --> 00:32:12.443
I used to work security for a guy
by the name of Manheim.

301
00:32:14.780 --> 00:32:17.866
Victor Manheim.
Have you heard of the name?

302
00:32:18.450 --> 00:32:21.411
Manheim. let me see... No.

303
00:32:22.413 --> 00:32:24.038
- He's a genius.
- Really?

304
00:32:24.540 --> 00:32:28.493
He has this habit of taking money
from the rich and giving it to the poor.

305
00:32:28.593 --> 00:32:31.296
- You've heard that story before...
- I've heard that story. Yeah.

306
00:32:33.132 --> 00:32:37.302
Now they're trying to find him.
But I'm not gonna help them.

307
00:32:37.970 --> 00:32:39.804
- Okay.
- So fuck 'em!

308
00:32:40.556 --> 00:32:42.223
Right. Fuck 'em.

309
00:32:45.102 --> 00:32:48.396
Portos. don't get killed.

310
00:32:48.564 --> 00:32:49.681
If you say so.

311
00:32:49.781 --> 00:32:51.983
Last time they killed a guy in here.

312
00:32:52.568 --> 00:32:55.153
they let his body rot for three days.

313
00:32:59.366 --> 00:33:01.034
And they canceled the prison dance.

314
00:33:05.789 --> 00:33:08.166
Wouldn't want to fuck up the prom.

315
00:33:14.131 --> 00:33:16.007
Morning. sir.

316
00:33:20.679 --> 00:33:23.181
That's another beautiful piece. sir.

317
00:33:24.725 --> 00:33:26.551
You lied to me.

318
00:33:26.651 --> 00:33:29.646
- I lied to you? I'm not sure what...
- No. no.

319
00:33:31.857 --> 00:33:33.107
You say nothing.

320
00:33:34.026 --> 00:33:37.904
What am I supposed to tell the client
about the man you killed?

321
00:33:38.322 --> 00:33:41.491
That he just jumped. like you said?

322
00:33:42.576 --> 00:33:46.496
This isn't a free-for-all.
We're paid to prevent him from jumping.

323
00:33:47.831 --> 00:33:50.917
And I can't get proof of life from a dead man.

324
00:33:51.669 --> 00:33:52.669
So...

325
00:33:54.046 --> 00:33:57.340
You will be docked
the entire price of the asset.

326
00:33:57.841 --> 00:34:01.386
The entire price of the asset
equals a month of my pay.

327
00:34:01.887 --> 00:34:05.390
Then you're lucky the man you killed
was not high value.

328
00:34:05.766 --> 00:34:07.183
That is all. Drake.

329
00:34:46.140 --> 00:34:49.142
Hey. Portos! Look at this.

330
00:34:50.811 --> 00:34:55.606
There's no sunrise. no sunset.
but still they pray all the time.

331
00:34:57.109 --> 00:34:58.609
Don't you find that interesting?

332
00:34:59.319 --> 00:35:00.403
Not really.

333
00:35:00.654 --> 00:35:04.282
You look like the kind of a guy
that finds things interesting.

334
00:35:04.616 --> 00:35:06.784
You've done time before?

335
00:35:09.288 --> 00:35:10.572
Why all the questions?

336
00:35:10.672 --> 00:35:12.457
That's how I learn things.

337
00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:14.459
You really ought to study somebody else.

338
00:35:16.003 --> 00:35:17.253
Portos!

339
00:35:18.589 --> 00:35:19.564
What?

340
00:35:19.664 --> 00:35:20.965
Need a favor?

341
00:35:23.635 --> 00:35:25.094
The favor man.

342
00:36:04.051 --> 00:36:08.346
For a man who is not interested.
you're doing a lot of looking.

343
00:36:13.811 --> 00:36:15.102
What do you need?

344
00:36:15.979 --> 00:36:18.648
I need to get into the isolation area.

345
00:36:19.650 --> 00:36:21.484
No. you really don't.

346
00:36:22.236 --> 00:36:25.863
Yeah. I really do. Call it a favor.

347
00:36:27.366 --> 00:36:28.366
Okay?

348
00:36:31.370 --> 00:36:32.370
Okay.

349
00:36:33.205 --> 00:36:34.205
Good.

350
00:36:41.213 --> 00:36:42.797
That's a favor?

351
00:36:42.923 --> 00:36:44.507
Sometimes favors hurt.

352
00:36:44.842 --> 00:36:46.242
Really?

353
00:36:46.392 --> 00:36:48.127
- Come on.
- Okay.

354
00:36:48.227 --> 00:36:49.720
Let's see what you can do.

355
00:36:49.930 --> 00:36:51.138
All right.

356
00:36:56.770 --> 00:36:58.304
You hit like a vegetarian.

357
00:36:58.404 --> 00:37:00.147
- Do I?
- You can do better than that.

358
00:37:03.777 --> 00:37:04.811
Come on.

359
00:37:04.911 --> 00:37:06.521
- All right.
- Let's see it.

360
00:37:06.621 --> 00:37:07.947
Try this.

361
00:37:11.326 --> 00:37:12.322
Hurt?

362
00:37:12.422 --> 00:37:13.862
That was good.

363
00:37:13.962 --> 00:37:15.371
Look what's coming!

364
00:37:22.796 --> 00:37:24.839
Relax. It's pretend.

365
00:37:27.259 --> 00:37:29.260
Guess boys will be boys.

366
00:37:30.804 --> 00:37:32.263
That's enough.

367
00:37:37.477 --> 00:37:39.846
Put them in the box! Now!

368
00:37:39.946 --> 00:37:41.439
You can thank me later.

369
00:38:34.368 --> 00:38:35.985
They knew he was tagged.

370
00:38:36.085 --> 00:38:38.237
Of course they knew.
Who do you think these guys are?

371
00:38:38.337 --> 00:38:41.741
What do you think. they're a bunch of
yahoos from one of those BOP facilities?

372
00:38:41.841 --> 00:38:46.170
This is the shadow world.
These guys. they invented this shit.

373
00:38:46.880 --> 00:38:48.506
Why do you think
they pay us all that money?

374
00:38:49.049 --> 00:38:50.249
Remember what the guidelines were.

375
00:38:50.349 --> 00:38:53.302
What the fuck are you talking about?
There are no guidelines.

376
00:38:54.346 --> 00:38:55.846
- Now. you call that CIA bitch.
- Hush...

377
00:39:00.477 --> 00:39:01.519
Motherfucker.

378
00:39:05.023 --> 00:39:07.024
All right. I'll make the call.

379
00:39:08.986 --> 00:39:12.530
Abigail. you got to keep him
away from me. all right?

380
00:39:29.214 --> 00:39:30.881
Give me your arm.

381
00:40:01.246 --> 00:40:02.280
You'll live.

382
00:40:02.380 --> 00:40:05.158
How does a doctor work in a place like this?

383
00:40:05.258 --> 00:40:07.376
Would you prefer
there wasn't a doctor here?

384
00:40:08.587 --> 00:40:09.754
Where is "here"?

385
00:40:12.924 --> 00:40:15.134
Hey. Doc. let's wrap it up.

386
00:40:34.112 --> 00:40:35.279
Doc...

387
00:40:36.782 --> 00:40:38.115
What did he ask you?

388
00:40:39.618 --> 00:40:40.618
He...

389
00:40:40.960 --> 00:40:45.456
Wanted to know how his dehydration
compared to the other detainees.

390
00:40:47.083 --> 00:40:48.367
And what did you tell him?

391
00:40:48.467 --> 00:40:50.002
I don't care.

392
00:40:51.755 --> 00:40:53.756
That's what I told him.

393
00:40:58.804 --> 00:41:00.054
Get him out of there.

394
00:41:16.530 --> 00:41:18.781
Did you find
what you were looking for in the box?

395
00:41:25.288 --> 00:41:30.000
All prisoners back to their cells.
All prisoners back to their cells.

396
00:41:44.224 --> 00:41:47.101
Who were you
before you came in here. Portos?

397
00:41:49.062 --> 00:41:52.306
You're always watching the room.
always watching everything.

398
00:41:52.406 --> 00:41:54.900
- Are you asking what I used to do?
- Yeah.

399
00:41:55.694 --> 00:41:57.945
I'll tell you. but I need a little favor.

400
00:41:58.196 --> 00:41:59.272
Fuck that.

401
00:41:59.372 --> 00:42:01.282
All right. don't do it.

402
00:42:01.700 --> 00:42:04.869
All right. I'm listening.
What's the favor this time?

403
00:42:05.370 --> 00:42:08.372
I need a piece of metal.
about three inches wide.

404
00:42:08.999 --> 00:42:10.499
Round. smooth.

405
00:42:11.334 --> 00:42:15.546
No problem. I'll hit the Home Depot.
and I'll be right back. Okay?

406
00:42:17.507 --> 00:42:21.719
If you get me that piece of metal.
I might be able to get you out of here.

407
00:42:29.227 --> 00:42:31.312
Tell Hobbes I want to talk.

408
00:42:34.733 --> 00:42:39.278
Interrogation. ready for inmate.
Interrogation. ready for inmate.

409
00:42:39.529 --> 00:42:42.031
You've been here six months now.
Mr. Rottmayer.

410
00:42:44.868 --> 00:42:46.869
So you know how this works.

411
00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:50.414
Ten seconds.

412
00:42:53.376 --> 00:42:55.252
Where is Victor Manheim?

413
00:42:55.921 --> 00:42:58.623
You know. to many people. he is a hero.

414
00:42:58.723 --> 00:43:00.049
Nine seconds.

415
00:43:00.467 --> 00:43:01.834
Do you have a pencil and a piece of paper?

416
00:43:01.934 --> 00:43:03.260
Eight seconds.

417
00:43:03.595 --> 00:43:04.929
I could draw you a map.

418
00:43:06.431 --> 00:43:07.506
Of what?

419
00:43:07.606 --> 00:43:09.558
Where you could find him.

420
00:43:19.778 --> 00:43:23.314
When I was a kid.
I always wanted to be an artist.

421
00:43:23.414 --> 00:43:25.783
My God. you are pushing it.

422
00:43:26.409 --> 00:43:28.619
Problem was. I had no talent.

423
00:43:29.245 --> 00:43:30.488
Six seconds.

424
00:43:30.588 --> 00:43:33.123
I tried and I tried and I tried...

425
00:43:33.333 --> 00:43:34.333
Five...

426
00:43:35.460 --> 00:43:36.869
Do you ever have dreams?

427
00:43:36.969 --> 00:43:37.995
Four...

428
00:43:38.095 --> 00:43:39.254
Or did you always want to be...

429
00:43:39.673 --> 00:43:40.706
- ...this?
- Two...

430
00:43:40.806 --> 00:43:42.174
- One...
- Done.

431
00:43:46.096 --> 00:43:47.972
Look. There.

432
00:43:51.643 --> 00:43:52.893
I told you.

433
00:43:54.312 --> 00:43:55.688
No talent.

434
00:43:57.691 --> 00:44:01.318
The records indicate
that you are a highly intelligent man.

435
00:44:02.821 --> 00:44:07.066
As such. I would have expected you to see
the situation and understand it for what it is.

436
00:44:07.166 --> 00:44:11.237
In here. you have no control
over any part of your life.

437
00:44:11.337 --> 00:44:13.406
except your breathing.

438
00:44:13.506 --> 00:44:15.165
And you just lost that privilege.

439
00:44:15.333 --> 00:44:16.375
Get him down!

440
00:44:52.203 --> 00:44:53.245
Keep going.

441
00:44:59.002 --> 00:45:00.169
Enough.

442
00:45:43.421 --> 00:45:44.671
What happened?

443
00:45:45.215 --> 00:45:47.925
Nothing. I'm still here.

444
00:45:51.554 --> 00:45:52.888
Now it's your turn.

445
00:45:56.101 --> 00:45:58.560
I break out of prisons for a living.

446
00:45:59.229 --> 00:46:00.429
For the past eight years.

447
00:46:00.529 --> 00:46:03.315
I've been breaking out of facilities for
the Federal Bureau of Prisons.

448
00:46:04.609 --> 00:46:08.487
I think Hobbes used my reports
to make this place unbreakable.

449
00:46:09.114 --> 00:46:12.574
Someone wanted this place tested.
but it was a set-up.

450
00:46:13.076 --> 00:46:17.029
They wanted to bury me.
I don't know who. but I'm gonna find out.

451
00:46:17.129 --> 00:46:19.748
I need you to set up another diversion.

452
00:46:20.792 --> 00:46:22.034
What now?

453
00:46:22.134 --> 00:46:24.044
You've got to go back in the box.

454
00:46:24.462 --> 00:46:25.746
No fucking way.

455
00:46:25.846 --> 00:46:28.132
Want to get outta here?

456
00:46:30.635 --> 00:46:32.803
Okay. I'll do it.

457
00:46:35.515 --> 00:46:39.143
But if I don't get out. I kill you.

458
00:46:40.145 --> 00:46:41.720
Fair enough.

459
00:46:41.820 --> 00:46:44.223
A successful breakout
depends on three things.

460
00:46:44.323 --> 00:46:46.433
layout. routine. and help.

461
00:46:46.533 --> 00:46:49.319
- But they've taken those away.
- For now.

462
00:46:50.321 --> 00:46:52.614
There's something under the box.
I think it's a conduit.

463
00:46:53.616 --> 00:46:56.451
If it is. how do you know where it goes?

464
00:47:01.666 --> 00:47:04.001
I don't. But I'm gonna find out.

465
00:47:05.170 --> 00:47:06.245
This is good.

466
00:47:06.345 --> 00:47:08.005
It's disgusting.

467
00:47:08.339 --> 00:47:12.418
The mind of a man confined works
differently than someone on the outside.

468
00:47:12.518 --> 00:47:16.096
He sees things different.
The architecture is vertical.

469
00:47:16.556 --> 00:47:19.466
The cell blocks. Babylon.
the box. the mess...

470
00:47:19.566 --> 00:47:22.519
Everything's in large vertical compartments.

471
00:47:25.315 --> 00:47:29.768
Best guess is they built out underground
in large natural fissures and caves.

472
00:47:29.868 --> 00:47:34.273
In a vertical structure. 70/30 says
whatever's under that box goes up.

473
00:47:34.373 --> 00:47:38.410
If I can get in there. follow where it goes.
I just might find my way to the surface.

474
00:47:40.371 --> 00:47:42.740
Let's say you're right. How do we cut metal?

475
00:47:42.840 --> 00:47:45.375
We don't cut. We don't cut at all.

476
00:47:46.085 --> 00:47:49.288
This place is subterranean.
There's moisture in the air.

477
00:47:49.388 --> 00:47:51.790
Whoever built this place
should have used aluminum rivets

478
00:47:51.890 --> 00:47:54.376
to hold those panels down.
but they used steel.

479
00:47:54.476 --> 00:47:56.136
Steel rusts over time.

480
00:47:58.389 --> 00:48:01.342
We apply that.
We'll concentrate the heat to those rivets

481
00:48:01.442 --> 00:48:04.561
and they'll expand
and snap right the fuck off.

482
00:48:05.271 --> 00:48:06.764
Concentrated heat?

483
00:48:06.864 --> 00:48:08.857
Yeah. from the piece of metal you gave me.

484
00:48:09.400 --> 00:48:13.020
You expose a toothpaste-polished piece of
metal to sunlight...

485
00:48:13.120 --> 00:48:14.980
- Or the lamps in the box.
- Right.

486
00:48:15.080 --> 00:48:18.984
At a hundred degrees centigrade.
steel expands .03 cubic centimeters

487
00:48:19.084 --> 00:48:21.779
and those rivets are gonna come right off.

488
00:48:21.879 --> 00:48:22.879
What?

489
00:48:23.915 --> 00:48:26.792
- You don't look that smart.
- You don't either.

490
00:48:27.293 --> 00:48:29.662
So most prisons
are built around small towns.

491
00:48:29.762 --> 00:48:33.540
No matter how remote.
they need supplies and a work force.

492
00:48:33.640 --> 00:48:35.000
If I can get to the surface.

493
00:48:35.100 --> 00:48:37.628
I'll know what it's going to take to get over
the wall. get out of here.

494
00:48:37.728 --> 00:48:40.722
But first I'm gonna need
that diversion in the box.

495
00:48:41.099 --> 00:48:42.841
How much time do you need?

496
00:48:42.941 --> 00:48:44.476
Three to five minutes.

497
00:48:49.941 --> 00:48:51.400
No problem.

498
00:49:12.297 --> 00:49:13.630
Step back.

499
00:49:14.299 --> 00:49:15.674
I know you.

500
00:49:18.678 --> 00:49:20.637
You don't know shit. you cunt-eater.

501
00:49:22.932 --> 00:49:24.182
Now step back.

502
00:49:24.434 --> 00:49:25.676
Now I remember.

503
00:49:25.776 --> 00:49:26.776
What?

504
00:49:27.437 --> 00:49:30.355
Your mother.
she was my favorite whore in Marrakesh.

505
00:49:31.441 --> 00:49:33.442
Man. she could polish a helmet!

506
00:50:08.728 --> 00:50:09.728
No!

507
00:50:19.405 --> 00:50:20.405
Hey!

508
00:51:29.934 --> 00:51:32.678
You're killing me! You're killing me!

509
00:51:32.778 --> 00:51:34.688
Bringing up box four. sir.

510
00:51:44.782 --> 00:51:46.700
Now. what is he up to?

511
00:51:53.791 --> 00:51:56.918
Hey! Shut the fuck up. you German dog!

512
00:52:01.632 --> 00:52:03.842
Master control. please advise.

513
00:52:10.766 --> 00:52:13.268
Just hold him till I get there.

514
00:52:16.606 --> 00:52:18.348
I've got a camera malfunction. box two.

515
00:52:18.448 --> 00:52:20.484
Roger that. Just reboot the system.

516
00:52:27.533 --> 00:52:28.533
Shit!

517
00:52:38.002 --> 00:52:39.336
Shut the fuck up!

518
00:52:43.007 --> 00:52:46.343
- Hey. Rottmayer. shut up!
- Restrain and drug him. sir?

519
00:52:46.511 --> 00:52:47.802
Not yet.

520
00:53:09.825 --> 00:53:11.368
Lights off. box four.

521
00:53:16.374 --> 00:53:17.582
Now open it.

522
00:53:25.216 --> 00:53:26.883
Rough day. Mr. Rottmayer?

523
00:55:35.054 --> 00:55:36.054
Let's get 'em.

524
00:55:36.305 --> 00:55:39.182
Here's what you should know. I don't care.

525
00:55:39.350 --> 00:55:41.843
Sooner or later you will tell me
what I want to know.

526
00:55:41.943 --> 00:55:44.354
It is inevitable. Like dying.

527
00:55:44.855 --> 00:55:49.101
But know this. there will come a point
where I don't give a shit

528
00:55:49.201 --> 00:55:53.605
about you or whatever the fuck
you think you're doing right now.

529
00:55:53.705 --> 00:55:56.700
So have a lovely day. Mr. Rottmayer.

530
00:56:32.069 --> 00:56:35.947
Emergency personnel to level two.
Emergency personnel to level two.

531
00:56:38.159 --> 00:56:39.155
Report?

532
00:56:39.255 --> 00:56:41.745
Valve breach on level two. sir.
Electrical malfunction.

533
00:56:50.296 --> 00:56:51.296
Sir?

534
00:56:51.922 --> 00:56:53.339
Get the assets out of there.

535
00:56:58.429 --> 00:57:00.029
Open up!

536
00:57:10.900 --> 00:57:13.276
Open the fucking door! Open the door!

537
00:57:39.804 --> 00:57:41.046
- Did you make it?
- Yeah.

538
00:57:41.146 --> 00:57:42.639
Where are we?

539
00:57:43.641 --> 00:57:45.517
- Where are we?
- I don't know!

540
00:57:46.143 --> 00:57:47.143
Fuck.

541
00:57:47.277 --> 00:57:48.248
They froze the check.

542
00:57:48.348 --> 00:57:49.554
What are we talking about here?

543
00:57:49.654 --> 00:57:51.981
The payment for Ray's services.
They froze the check.

544
00:57:54.026 --> 00:57:56.353
It's not frozen. it's on hold. All right?

545
00:57:56.453 --> 00:57:58.772
It's very common in
a $2.5 million transaction.

546
00:57:58.872 --> 00:58:02.859
No. Common would be a week. maybe
10 days. This has been way longer than that.

547
00:58:02.959 --> 00:58:05.787
Jesus. Abby. It's the federal government.

548
00:58:07.790 --> 00:58:09.366
You know how they work.

549
00:58:09.466 --> 00:58:10.437
Did you call that woman?

550
00:58:10.537 --> 00:58:12.577
Yeah. I called. Everything is fine.

551
00:58:12.677 --> 00:58:13.962
Then where is he?

552
00:58:15.339 --> 00:58:17.582
He is on the job that he was hired to do.

553
00:58:17.682 --> 00:58:19.968
So you're saying it's all good?

554
00:58:23.138 --> 00:58:24.422
It's all good.

555
00:58:24.522 --> 00:58:26.391
Where was the breach?

556
00:58:26.517 --> 00:58:29.386
The auxiliary ballast tank system
on the starboard side.

557
00:58:29.486 --> 00:58:32.597
Compartments five and seven
have been compromised.

558
00:58:32.697 --> 00:58:36.025
And that leads to
the ventilation shaft under box two.

559
00:58:38.195 --> 00:58:39.362
Portos.

560
00:58:51.876 --> 00:58:53.368
Yeah. they're full of rust.

561
00:58:53.468 --> 00:58:55.670
Water pressure must have
snapped them clean off.

562
00:58:58.048 --> 00:58:59.248
Maybe.

563
00:59:05.931 --> 00:59:07.799
Portos isn't his name. is it?

564
00:59:07.899 --> 00:59:09.467
Why wasn't I alerted?

565
00:59:09.567 --> 00:59:11.636
Look. it's like this.
There's a lot of people paying money

566
00:59:11.736 --> 00:59:14.639
to make sure that facility is unbreakable.

567
00:59:14.739 --> 00:59:17.517
It's Ray Breslin. The great Ray Breslin.

568
00:59:17.617 --> 00:59:20.186
He's there to prove
that not even he can get out.

569
00:59:20.286 --> 00:59:23.982
You make sure he stays there forever.
Do you have a problem with that?

570
00:59:24.082 --> 00:59:28.286
No. Not at all. Just the opposite.

571
00:59:28.495 --> 00:59:29.491
Fucker.

572
00:59:29.591 --> 00:59:31.990
All right. good. There's one more thing.

573
00:59:32.090 --> 00:59:36.620
The Chinese banks
have joined the Brazilians. the Russians.

574
00:59:36.720 --> 00:59:39.956
the English. the U.S. and the Swiss banks.

575
00:59:40.056 --> 00:59:44.002
They're all paying to find out
the whereabouts of this Manheim fellow.

576
00:59:44.102 --> 00:59:46.463
Word on the street
is that he has developed a program

577
00:59:46.563 --> 00:59:50.634
to turn the entire world banking system
into fucking confetti.

578
00:59:50.734 --> 00:59:53.219
Rottmayer worked with that asshole.
He knows where he is.

579
00:59:53.319 --> 00:59:55.889
Your job is to get that information
out of him.

580
00:59:55.989 --> 00:59:59.651
Well. it just so happens that since Breslin
has gotten closer to Rottmayer.

581
01:00:00.110 --> 01:00:04.697
Rottmayer has developed a new edge to
his defiance that wasn't there before.

582
01:00:04.949 --> 01:00:07.367
I think Breslin is to blame.

583
01:00:08.243 --> 01:00:09.694
Then break Breslin.

584
01:00:09.794 --> 01:00:11.329
Thank you.

585
01:00:13.123 --> 01:00:15.959
I have an assignment I know you'll enjoy.

586
01:00:44.154 --> 01:00:45.947
Get on your feet!

587
01:00:53.497 --> 01:00:55.123
Wakey. wakey...

588
01:01:03.632 --> 01:01:05.008
Talk to me.

589
01:01:05.676 --> 01:01:07.677
Come on. You must fight.

590
01:01:09.179 --> 01:01:10.579
Get up!

591
01:01:10.814 --> 01:01:11.848
Stay on your feet!

592
01:01:12.141 --> 01:01:13.800
If we're on a ship. we would know.

593
01:01:13.900 --> 01:01:14.900
No.

594
01:01:15.026 --> 01:01:19.264
Not if it was 1.000 feet long.
200 feet high. with stabilizers.

595
01:01:19.364 --> 01:01:21.190
We wouldn't know a damn thing.

596
01:01:22.192 --> 01:01:24.902
Wakey. wakey! Get him on his feet.

597
01:01:36.707 --> 01:01:40.118
- You can do it. Keep going.
- Come on. go. Move it!

598
01:01:40.218 --> 01:01:41.453
We can't get out of here.

599
01:01:41.553 --> 01:01:42.712
- Yes. we can.
- No!

600
01:01:45.841 --> 01:01:47.425
Get on your feet!

601
01:01:48.552 --> 01:01:49.794
You've got to stay strong.

602
01:01:49.894 --> 01:01:53.973
Back up! Back up! It's you I want. Move it!

603
01:01:57.895 --> 01:01:59.395
Piece of shit...

604
01:02:16.121 --> 01:02:17.830
Stop it now. Drake.

605
01:02:36.100 --> 01:02:38.851
Don't give up. Don't let them break you.

606
01:02:39.645 --> 01:02:42.396
What made you want to
spend your life in prison?

607
01:02:44.900 --> 01:02:47.610
Tell me. What made you do it?

608
01:02:50.155 --> 01:02:51.447
Tell me!

609
01:02:59.790 --> 01:03:02.458
I was a lawyer. Prosecutor.

610
01:03:03.794 --> 01:03:07.797
A man I put away made a promise to me.

611
01:03:08.340 --> 01:03:11.634
This man thought about that promise
every day for three years.

612
01:03:12.636 --> 01:03:14.762
planning his way out of prison.

613
01:03:15.639 --> 01:03:18.391
planning on how
he was gonna keep his word.

614
01:03:20.352 --> 01:03:22.562
Taking a man's life is nothing.

615
01:03:23.772 --> 01:03:25.106
Taking his heart...

616
01:03:26.817 --> 01:03:28.484
That's everything. isn't it?

617
01:03:33.991 --> 01:03:35.074
Everything.

618
01:03:45.294 --> 01:03:48.838
You see. putting people in prison
wasn't good enough.

619
01:03:49.965 --> 01:03:51.924
And I had to... I wanted to

620
01:03:53.010 --> 01:03:55.178
make sure they stayed in there.
didn't get out.

621
01:03:55.721 --> 01:03:58.848
I understand. I have a daughter.

622
01:04:00.225 --> 01:04:03.311
Never forget them. You have a choice.

623
01:04:03.729 --> 01:04:05.021
You can die in here.

624
01:04:05.355 --> 01:04:08.733
or you can get out with me
and punish who put you here.

625
01:04:10.194 --> 01:04:11.319
You hear me?

626
01:04:12.237 --> 01:04:13.237
Yeah.

627
01:04:21.371 --> 01:04:22.989
Good news and bad news.

628
01:04:23.089 --> 01:04:26.910
I was thinking about that first meeting.
privatized incarceration.

629
01:04:27.010 --> 01:04:30.455
Off the grid. international profile.
And I started digging.

630
01:04:30.555 --> 01:04:34.959
Code name. The Tomb.
Completely for profit. totally illegal.

631
01:04:35.059 --> 01:04:39.055
Run by ex-military assholes and
Blackwater rejects. You know. bad dudes.

632
01:04:39.514 --> 01:04:41.299
If Ray is anywhere. it's here.

633
01:04:41.399 --> 01:04:43.226
Where is "here"?

634
01:04:43.727 --> 01:04:45.228
That's the bad news.

635
01:04:47.356 --> 01:04:49.065
I don't know.

636
01:04:55.239 --> 01:04:57.156
No access to any layout.

637
01:04:59.034 --> 01:05:00.743
No blind times.

638
01:05:03.372 --> 01:05:06.249
We're in the middle of the fucking ocean.

639
01:05:06.625 --> 01:05:09.669
But I'll be damned if I didn't find a routine.

640
01:05:10.545 --> 01:05:12.964
They scramble the guard shifts
so they're never the same.

641
01:05:13.757 --> 01:05:17.551
But they can't change the routine of
the guards themselves.

642
01:05:17.928 --> 01:05:21.214
We don't know when they start.
We don't know when they end.

643
01:05:21.314 --> 01:05:24.600
But I do know
where they're gonna be based on habit.

644
01:05:24.935 --> 01:05:28.846
See that guy coming down the stairs?
See how he walks all pigeon-toed?

645
01:05:28.946 --> 01:05:29.917
The Duck.

646
01:05:30.017 --> 01:05:34.018
Yeah. The Duck always works with the guy
scratching the back of his neck.

647
01:05:34.118 --> 01:05:35.318
Hives.

648
01:05:36.571 --> 01:05:37.822
Yeah. Hives.

649
01:05:38.073 --> 01:05:41.234
When Duck and Hives work together.
they always do a circle.

650
01:05:41.334 --> 01:05:43.987
They may do it at random times of day.
It doesn't matter when they do it.

651
01:05:44.087 --> 01:05:48.249
it always ends up being 128 strides.
then they split up. Watch.

652
01:05:49.293 --> 01:05:51.411
Now they each take a side.

653
01:05:51.511 --> 01:05:55.464
Duck walks 63 strides. Hives 65.
Then they meet up at the top.

654
01:05:57.009 --> 01:06:00.670
The guard down there at the bottom.
the heavy-set guy. he doesn't move much.

655
01:06:00.770 --> 01:06:04.507
My guess is he's been here a while
and only does what he has to do.

656
01:06:04.607 --> 01:06:05.641
Louisa.

657
01:06:07.185 --> 01:06:08.261
Louisa?

658
01:06:08.361 --> 01:06:10.730
His fat ass reminds me of my first girlfriend.

659
01:06:12.816 --> 01:06:13.816
Nice.

660
01:06:14.651 --> 01:06:17.061
That guard over there
could be a problem for us.

661
01:06:17.161 --> 01:06:18.396
He's always looking around.

662
01:06:18.496 --> 01:06:20.781
- The Chicken Man.
- Chicken Man. right.

663
01:06:22.159 --> 01:06:25.111
My guess. Chickie's new here.
Does everything by the book.

664
01:06:25.211 --> 01:06:27.697
- How do you know when the shift ends?
- I don't.

665
01:06:27.797 --> 01:06:31.534
But around this time. your girlfriend
Louisa starts looking at her watch.

666
01:06:31.634 --> 01:06:33.669
My guess. it's lunchtime.

667
01:06:36.715 --> 01:06:38.416
Welcome back.

668
01:06:38.516 --> 01:06:39.675
Thanks.

669
01:06:40.635 --> 01:06:41.919
Now that we've got the routine.

670
01:06:42.019 --> 01:06:44.889
we just gotta ask the good doctor
where the hell we are.

671
01:06:56.151 --> 01:06:58.519
I'm not permitted
to give you anything for the pain.

672
01:06:58.619 --> 01:07:00.196
so don't request it.

673
01:07:00.697 --> 01:07:03.407
You're a doctor. You took an oath.

674
01:07:04.076 --> 01:07:06.535
"According to my ability and judgment.

675
01:07:06.870 --> 01:07:09.830
"I'll protect my patients
from harm and injustice."

676
01:07:18.382 --> 01:07:19.882
What you're doing here is wrong.

677
01:07:24.012 --> 01:07:26.347
What exactly is it you want from me?

678
01:07:26.556 --> 01:07:28.557
I want to know where the hell I am.

679
01:07:43.407 --> 01:07:44.407
Guards!

680
01:07:49.079 --> 01:07:50.913
It's okay. It's under control.

681
01:07:51.331 --> 01:07:52.623
Put him back here.

682
01:08:03.802 --> 01:08:04.927
Sorry.

683
01:08:19.443 --> 01:08:20.776
- So...
- No.

684
01:08:21.611 --> 01:08:22.854
Got to push him harder.

685
01:08:22.954 --> 01:08:24.856
Push him. we'll lose him.

686
01:08:24.956 --> 01:08:26.482
No other options?

687
01:08:26.582 --> 01:08:27.825
Plan B.

688
01:08:29.494 --> 01:08:31.745
You always gotta have a Plan B.

689
01:08:38.628 --> 01:08:39.753
Did you get it?

690
01:08:50.474 --> 01:08:52.516
Now I need his glasses.

691
01:10:05.215 --> 01:10:08.175
Sir? You want to take a look at this?

692
01:10:13.890 --> 01:10:15.975
- What's this?
- It's a sextant.

693
01:10:18.395 --> 01:10:19.845
Of course it is.

694
01:10:19.945 --> 01:10:22.974
It works.
You spot the North Star with the horizon.

695
01:10:23.074 --> 01:10:25.401
But it will only give us half of our location.

696
01:10:29.656 --> 01:10:31.198
Bring Breslin.

697
01:10:32.993 --> 01:10:36.320
I'll explain how it works later.
but first we've got to get it topside.

698
01:10:36.420 --> 01:10:37.705
Watch out.

699
01:10:53.555 --> 01:10:56.515
Welcome to your new home. Mr. Breslin.

700
01:10:57.684 --> 01:10:59.059
Section E.

701
01:10:59.686 --> 01:11:01.596
Waiting for inmates.

702
01:11:01.696 --> 01:11:03.180
You know who I am?

703
01:11:03.280 --> 01:11:04.773
I do now.

704
01:11:05.525 --> 01:11:08.944
I've studied your work very closely.
It's quite brilliant.

705
01:11:10.155 --> 01:11:14.617
As a matter of fact. it's what I used as
a reference guide in designing this facility.

706
01:11:15.201 --> 01:11:16.902
If you know who I am. let me go.

707
01:11:17.002 --> 01:11:19.155
No. no. no. no. Mr. Breslin.

708
01:11:19.255 --> 01:11:22.166
That's not how this works. Not this time.

709
01:11:22.375 --> 01:11:26.203
You see. the people who paid for
you to be here want you here forever.

710
01:11:26.303 --> 01:11:29.298
And knowing that.
and knowing who you are.

711
01:11:30.300 --> 01:11:32.426
well. who you were...

712
01:11:34.220 --> 01:11:36.505
I can't have you
communicating with Rottmayer.

713
01:11:36.605 --> 01:11:38.799
or anybody else. for that matter.

714
01:11:38.899 --> 01:11:42.303
This is the reality. And there's no way out.

715
01:11:42.403 --> 01:11:43.929
This can go two ways.

716
01:11:44.029 --> 01:11:46.182
You let me go
and I'll pretend this never happened.

717
01:11:46.282 --> 01:11:50.653
You don't. and I'll burn this fucking place
to the ground on my way out.

718
01:11:52.072 --> 01:11:55.149
Effective right now. no mess. no rec time.

719
01:11:55.249 --> 01:11:57.618
and no showers.

720
01:11:58.745 --> 01:12:01.038
I can get you Victor Manheim.

721
01:12:02.957 --> 01:12:04.833
Rottmayer trusts me.

722
01:12:06.544 --> 01:12:08.128
So you say.

723
01:12:08.963 --> 01:12:09.997
Not good enough.

724
01:12:10.097 --> 01:12:12.166
What have you got to lose?
Finding him has got to be worth

725
01:12:12.266 --> 01:12:14.718
a lot more than what you were paid for me.
right. Hobbes?

726
01:12:14.928 --> 01:12:16.587
It's a nice idea. but

727
01:12:16.687 --> 01:12:20.224
as it stands right now.
I'm in line to get both.

728
01:12:20.934 --> 01:12:24.478
You'll never break Rottmayer.
He'll die before he turns.

729
01:12:25.188 --> 01:12:28.232
I'm your only chance to get what you want.

730
01:12:33.571 --> 01:12:37.942
I want Manheim and his whole network.
Names. Locations in real time.

731
01:12:38.042 --> 01:12:41.161
Get that. If it checks out. I'll let you go.
But know this.

732
01:12:41.413 --> 01:12:44.115
You tell me every word
that you and Rottmayer share.

733
01:12:44.215 --> 01:12:47.292
or I will personally
pull the fucking life out of you.

734
01:12:48.002 --> 01:12:49.545
Fair enough.

735
01:12:55.969 --> 01:12:57.428
So what happened?

736
01:12:57.554 --> 01:12:59.138
I'm playing you.

737
01:13:01.349 --> 01:13:03.843
Last night Rottmayer told me
he started his network

738
01:13:03.943 --> 01:13:06.395
with five guys from his hometown.

739
01:13:07.397 --> 01:13:09.765
He said he could trust his life to these guys.

740
01:13:09.865 --> 01:13:11.316
Give Javed the sextant.

741
01:13:11.901 --> 01:13:14.729
Show him how to use it.
Tell him it's his ticket outta here.

742
01:13:14.829 --> 01:13:17.406
Javed. He'd rather see us dead.

743
01:13:17.699 --> 01:13:19.650
He'll be the last one they suspect.

744
01:13:19.750 --> 01:13:20.860
He bragged how his network

745
01:13:20.960 --> 01:13:23.863
caused the bank collapse
in Iceland six years ago.

746
01:13:23.963 --> 01:13:27.499
I don't give a shit about six years ago.
I want to know where he is now.

747
01:13:46.519 --> 01:13:48.145
You want to die?

748
01:13:49.314 --> 01:13:51.231
You want to get out?

749
01:13:58.782 --> 01:13:59.948
Today.

750
01:14:02.494 --> 01:14:04.028
They're plotting an escape.

751
01:14:04.128 --> 01:14:05.537
An escape?

752
01:14:06.581 --> 01:14:08.574
Really? Who and when?

753
01:14:08.674 --> 01:14:10.375
I don't know all the details.

754
01:14:11.961 --> 01:14:12.995
Just some.

755
01:14:13.095 --> 01:14:15.589
Well. tell me the details you know.

756
01:14:18.802 --> 01:14:20.803
You give me things first.

757
01:14:24.390 --> 01:14:28.602
Mr. Alfredo. Afridi.
or whatever the fuck your name is...

758
01:14:28.978 --> 01:14:33.482
Your opium drug cartel friends
have paid a lot of money for you to be here.

759
01:14:36.402 --> 01:14:38.862
Of course they did. those fucks.

760
01:14:39.280 --> 01:14:41.114
So aside from your freedom.

761
01:14:42.909 --> 01:14:44.535
what else can I give you?

762
01:14:45.328 --> 01:14:48.239
I want the guards to leave my people alone.

763
01:14:48.339 --> 01:14:49.998
The Holy Koran...

764
01:14:51.501 --> 01:14:53.335
I want one in my cell.

765
01:14:54.045 --> 01:14:56.463
And I want to say the name of Allah

766
01:14:57.090 --> 01:15:00.175
and the prophet Mohammed in the open air.

767
01:15:02.178 --> 01:15:04.263
I want to be seen by my God

768
01:15:05.723 --> 01:15:08.183
when I say my evening prayers.

769
01:15:09.853 --> 01:15:11.061
That's all?

770
01:15:11.604 --> 01:15:13.063
That's all.

